 ### [3-axis rasterization voxelization](2480-3-axis-rasterization-voxelization.md)
-Produces a 6-separating voxelization of 3D input geometry by rasterizing primitives along three axis-aligned projection directions in three separate passes. It is distinct from 26-separating methods by generating a sparser voxel set sufficient for applications using 6-connected ray marching. It is equivalent to using a "crosshairs" intersection target and is notably robust for curved primitives, requiring only point-depth evaluations. Choose this method when a sparse, 6-connected voxel boundary is required.
