 ### [Chunked UV Rasterization with Face ID Storage](2598-chunked-uv-rasterization-with-face-id-storage.md)
-Rasterizes a 3D mesh in 2D UV space to generate voxel data, using memory-friendly chunking to handle large geometries. It differs from [3-axis rasterization voxelization](2480-3-axis-rasterization-voxelization.md) by projecting onto a single UV plane per pass and storing face identifiers to enable precise 3D position interpolation, rather than relying on depth buffers or multiple axis projections. It addresses VRAM limitations by processing faces in batches. Choose this method for large meshes where VRAM is limited and precise surface position interpolation is needed.
